  "summary": "This paper compares three models for predicting low stock prices of CRDB and NMB using 2,525 data points per bank: LSTM, MLR, and a variational quantum neural network (VQNN) built with PennyLane and Quantum Dense. The reported VQNN metrics include RMSE as low as 0.1231 and 0.6522, MAPE as low as 0.1463, and R2 up to 0.9945, but the paper concludes that the classical LSTM and especially MLR are more accurate overall than the VQNN.",
